}
}
}

Edge cases from logs/duel/duels.jsonl:
- zero duels: all duel_records and totals have rows_judged=0, wins=losses=ties=unparsed=0; quality_gate.gate_passed=false when metric_value < decided_min
- UNPARSED winner rows: increment unparsed using winner field value "UNPARSED"
- TIE rows: increment ties using winner field value "TIE"
- missing price: prices still required in schema; set source to "UNPROVEN" when absent from price receipt
- a cost of exactly zero: allow a_cost=0 or b_cost=0 as number >=0; no effect on counts
- task shape outside known list: ignore row; duel_records keys restricted by additionalProperties=false using rubric field to map to one of adversarial-review/schema-design/planning/code-analysis/grading (mapping rule UNPROVEN)

Idempotent migration: read entire logs/duel/duels.jsonl each run; aggregate per model_id (a_model when swap=false else b_model) using ask_id as dedup key in a transient set before counting winner/a_model/b_model/swap/rubric into duel_records and totals; write fresh router_families.json from full aggregates plus provenance.ledger_sha256 and provenance.row_count; never append incrementally.

Validation predicates:
- every duel_record.rows_judged equals wins+losses+ties+unparsed and same equality holds for totals
- provenance.row_count equals exact line count of logs/duel/duels.jsonl
- quality_gate.gate_passed equals (metric_value >= decided_min)

